From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:31:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Battery saver: let background tools hold EmulationStation
 awake

The aggressive battery saver stops EmulationStation with SIGSTOP when the
screen dims. Its HTTP API (port 1234) then accepts connections but never
answers, so a background tool waits until the user wakes the device (a
sync once hung 53 min), and nothing tells the tool that ES is stopped.

Move the saver into knulli-aggressive-saver, following development's
version (lock, state file, only resume what it stopped), and add holds:
"knulli-aggressive-saver run NAME -- CMD" keeps ES running while CMD
runs; paused games stay paused and the saver stops ES again afterwards.
A hold whose process is gone is dropped. /var/run/emulationstation.suspended
holds the ES process group while ES is stopped, and "state" reports it.
The idle and active hooks keep their inline code as a fallback.

Also fix the scraper pause: the scraper-start/stop hooks wrote
/var/run/batterysaver, a folder the battery saver never reads, so a long
scrape could be frozen.
---
 .../etc/idlewatcher/active.d/01active-hooks   |   8 +
 .../etc/idlewatcher/idle.d/01idle-hooks       |   8 +
 .../fsoverlay/usr/bin/knulli-aggressive-saver | 228 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../scraper-start/battery-saver-pause.sh      |   4 +-
 .../scraper-stop/battery-saver-unpause.sh     |   2 +-
 5 files changed, 247 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 board/fsoverlay/usr/bin/knulli-aggressive-saver

